      authorEn: 'Thomas Nagel', authorPt: 'Thomas Nagel', authorEs: 'Thomas Nagel',
      textEn: 'The great cognitive shift is an expansion of consciousness from the perspectival form contained in the lives of particular creatures to an objective, world-encompassing form that exists both individually and intersubjectively. It was originally a biological evolutionary process, and in our species it has become a collective cultural process as well. Each of our lives is a part of the lengthy process of the universe gradually waking up and becoming aware of itself.',
